  "caveats": [
    "This is a newly adopted independent three-leaf design. All 16 images were newly generated for this branch; the two legacy root images are retained unchanged and are not used in this set. Earlier held branches are not reused.",
    "New anatomy: three separate thin fan leaves meet one stem-top node, with a higher central blade and two lower lateral blades; one upright stem terminates in two connected broad root-foot masses. Two eyes exist only on the central front leaf surface. No arms, wings or tail.",
    "The legacy curved seedpod, four root legs and coiled tail are not identity requirements of this redesign. The selected normal front S defines the new visual identity. Each selected pixel image was generated using only its own direction normal as the image reference.",
    "Visible eyes are two in S/SE/SW, one edge eye in E/W and zero in NE/N/NW. Physical leaf count is three; leaf visibility and overlap depend on direction, and occluded leaf parts are inferred.",
    "NE/NW and E/W expose unequal amounts of leaf face. These are artistic approximate directional projections; exact 45-degree spacing, hidden attachment depth and measured 3D consistency have not been proved.",
    "Pixel rendering simplifies leaf edges into angular steps, emphasizes veins and outlines, and has minor proportion differences including a slightly taller S silhouette. The fixed palette roles are green leaves (#9FB86F), brown stem/feet (#C48A63) and cream veins (#EBDBC5), with generated lighting shades rather than exact flat-color equivalence.",
    "Runtime and device-scale rendering have not been tested."
  ],
  "publication_status": "approved_for_draft_review"
}
